Exercise 6.1: Incorrect String comparison.

Answer: == compares object references not the characters in the strings. Since each new String("Java")
        creates a separate String object, "first == second" will be false, even both contain the same text.

Exercise 6.2: Array index.

Answer: The array has length 3, so its valid indexes are 0, 1, and 2. With i <= numbers.length,
        the loop tries to access index 3 causing an ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException.

